# Discrete repo — line-ending normalisation rules.
#
# Why: Phase 22 live smoke (2026-05-12) caught a real failure on
# unity_scene.lua. AOBMaker plugin's CE-side InjectTableFile path
# normalises CRLF→LF inside CE's StringStream / TableFile, but
# verifies the post-write Stream.Size against the pre-normalisation
# byte count. A CRLF-having file mismatches by exactly one byte per
# line ending, fails verification, and the whole bridge-inject
# pipeline aborts.
#
# Discrete itself is fine on either line ending — the only consumer
# that cares is the AOBMaker pipe round-trip. But the safe default is
# LF everywhere (that's what the embedded resources encode, what the
# tests assume, and what every existing scripts/*.lua except the
# accidentally-CRLF unity_scene.lua already shipped with).
#
# git config core.autocrlf is honoured per-machine; this file
# OVERRIDES it for the patterns listed below so the in-tree state is
# deterministic regardless of contributor environment.

# Default: every text file LF on checkout AND in the index. Binary
# detection via git heuristics (e.g. .png stays binary).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt + braces for the file types Discrete cares most about.
*.lua  text eol=lf
*.cs   text eol=lf
*.cpp  text eol=lf
*.c    text eol=lf
*.h    text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.axaml text eol=lf
*.xaml  text eol=lf

# PowerShell + Windows scripts are also fine as LF (PowerShell 7+
# parses both; build.cmd is the lone exception — Windows shell needs
# CRLF or it breaks line-continuation).
*.ps1  text eol=lf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.bat  text eol=crlf

# Build artifacts / generated content / vendored binaries stay binary.
*.dll  binary
*.exe  binary
*.pdb  binary
*.lib  binary
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.zip  binary
